vexations 

next generation programming language.

vexations is a new approach to programming. we utilize a Rust workspace
to host a compiler library for efficient code compilation and diagnostics
for the vexations language, the cli tool for the compiler library, and the test
infrastructure for the compiler and the language.

the project uses AFL (American Fuzzy Lop) to extensively fuzz unsafe compiler
targets, and cargo-tarpaulin via Github Workflows for code coverage
instrumentation.

---

vexations language

vexations is the second iteration of the mumbo language idea. currently,
the specifications are not public, but the compiler is fully open source;
feel free to read through the sources.

---

building

build using Cargo.

building the project from scratch requires a nightly Rust compiler and the
Cargo infrastructure.

run cargo build --release -p vexations-cli to compile the CLI component of
the compiler.

there are provided shell scripts for development in the bash directory
written in GNU bash.

run ./bash/test.bash to test all the test targets within /tests. run
./bash/llvm-ir.bash and ./bash/asm.bash to generate intermediate compilation
artifacts for in-depth analysis of the codegen for the compiler itself. run
./bash/tarpaulin.bash to generate a local coverage report. requires
cargo-tarpaulin. run ./bash/fuzz-lexer.bash to fuzz the lexer target using AFL.
check out https://rust-fuzz.github.io/book/afl.html for more details on how to
get AFL working.

---

AI policy

no AI.

here at vexations we do not tolerate the use of AI when writing code. the only
semi-acceptable use of AI is **meta-management** of legacy/broken build/test/CI
infrastructures when all side effects of such methods are thoroughly human
vetted.

the vexations compiler currently does not and MUST never contain any AI
generated code or comments.

---

contributing

no contribution.

this project is open source but closed contribution. we don't accept
contributions until further notice.

